# Identity normalisation for git (see `man gitmailmap`).
#
# Collapses the name/e-mail spellings a single contributor committed under, so
# that history-derived tooling — git shortlog, git blame, and the per-document
# attribution records (tool/attribution) — credits each person once.
#
# This is a seed covering the duplicates visible in `git shortlog -sne` as of
# the first attribution run; extend it as new variants appear. Each entry maps
# the variant(s) on the right to the canonical identity on the left.

# Multiple e-mails per person
